WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:08.064
If your workstation runs on chained extension boards, you have a safety problem waiting to happen.

00:00:08.664 --> 00:00:12.978
Trailing cables cause trips, damaged plugs and overloaded sockets.

00:00:13.258 --> 00:00:18.446
And when power is out of reach, operators stretch, or unplug one tool to use another.

00:00:19.046 --> 00:00:21.346
There are four ways to bring power to the bench.

00:00:21.626 --> 00:00:26.276
A horizontal power rail runs between two uprights and pivots to face you.

00:00:26.556 --> 00:00:29.523
A vertical power strip runs up a single upright.

00:00:29.803 --> 00:00:34.874
An outlet strip mounts on or under a Base worktop, with 8 outlets and a breaker.

00:00:35.154 --> 00:00:39.431
And a powered instrument riser gives sockets at the back of a Scitec bench.

00:00:39.711 --> 00:00:43.304
Always switch off and unplug equipment before moving a rail.

00:00:43.904 --> 00:00:47.852
Furnisys power rails and strips use 15 amp switch sockets.

00:00:48.132 --> 00:00:52.478
The horizontal power rail is the most specified option in our projects.

00:00:53.078 --> 00:00:54.803
Bring power to the work, safely.

00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:57.264
How many extension boards are in your area?

00:00:57.544 --> 00:01:01.010
Comment below, and next, compare task lighting options.

00:01:01.610 --> 00:01:05.855
Furnisys: complete workspace systems, planned around your process.

